Three things to note before the handoff:
1. r116 is still running on the board (codex is adding logs to reproduce the hang, with a 2-hour time limit). After it finishes, the middleware on the board may have been replaced with a fixed version or rolled back — go by its report. The report is in docs/proposals/evidence/stall-onboard-20261011/, and the branch is feat/r116-stall-onboard.
2. The code hasn't been backed up yet: the backup repo is at da6c256. After plugging in the external drive, run git push origin --all.
3. Disk and swap: this Mac currently has 64 GB free, but the ~25 GB swap generated during export hasn't been released yet — it will only be reclaimed after a reboot. If the person taking over continues r114's export, it's best to reboot once first.

